   118	\subsection{Models}
   119	
   120	We evaluate a total of 32+ models spanning \textbf{0.6B to 671B parameters
   121	across 5 model families}, organized into three tiers by compute scale:
   122	
   123	\paragraph{Small scale (0.6B--8B).}
   124	Qwen3-0.6B-Instruct, Qwen3.5-4B, Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B,
   125	Llama-3.2-1B, Llama-3.2-3B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct.
   126	
   127	\paragraph{Mid scale (14B--32B).}
   128	Qwen3-14B, Qwen3-30B-A3B (MoE), Qwen3-32B, Qwen3.5-27B,
   129	GPT-OSS-20b, Kimi-K2 (selected scale points).
   130	
   131	\paragraph{Larger-model support probes (70B--671B).}
   132	Qwen3-235B-A22B (MoE), DeepSeek-V3.1 ($\approx$671B total / 37B active),
   133	Nemotron-120B, and selected 397B-class MoE architectures.
   134	Larger-model probes are evaluated via the Tinker API in inference mode
   135	with standardized generation parameters; LoRA fine-tuning at this
   136	scale is conducted on selected checkpoints (see Section~\ref{sec:frontier}).
   137	
   138	\paragraph{Model family coverage.}
   139	The audit corpus covers (1) \textbf{Qwen3}: a dense family from 0.6B to 32B;
   140	(2) \textbf{Qwen3.5}: an improved series including 4B and 27B;
   141	(3) \textbf{Llama-3.x}: Meta's 1B--8B instruction-tuned models;
   142	(4) \textbf{DeepSeek-V3.1}: a frontier MoE optimized for reasoning;
   143	(5) \textbf{Nemotron-120B}: NVIDIA's dense frontier model;
   144	and emerging architectures \textbf{GPT-OSS-20b} and \textbf{Kimi-K2}.
   145	
   146	\subsection{Training Protocol}
   147	
   148	All experiments use LoRA~\cite{hu2022lora} with rank 32, learning rate $10^{-4}$,
   149	Adam optimizer ($\beta_1=0.9$, $\beta_2=0.95$, $\epsilon=10^{-8}$).
   150	
   151	\paragraph{Seed management.} Only selected TRL baselines and the GSM8K
   152	held-out evaluation use five seeds; the majority of Tinker runs are
   153	single-seed.  When seeds are set, we use
   154	$\{42, 123, 456, 789, 1024\}$ for Python \texttt{random},
   155	NumPy, PyTorch, and CUDA backends.
