    10	\section*{Statistical Protocol Disclosure (Authoritative)}
    11	\label{sec:stat_protocol_disclosure}
    12	
    13	The paper contains several correction regimes (a 5-test family-wise
    14	Bonferroni on the capability-claim table, a 20-test Benjamini--Hochberg
    15	sweep on descriptive effect sizes, a 38-test global Bonferroni on the full
    16	battery reported in this appendix, and a separate 5-test effect-table
    17	correction).  To prevent protocol ambiguity we designate the following as
    18	the \emph{primary inferential protocol} for claim verification:
    19	
    20	\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=2em,itemsep=2pt]
    21	    \item \textbf{Primary family} (5 tests): paired held-out GSM8K control,
    22	    Qwen PPO-vs-GRPO last-10 contrast, Llama PPO-vs-GRPO last-10 contrast,
    23	    Tinker-vs-TRL matched-stack 17$\times$ gap, and TRL-GRPO seed-variance
    24	    check. Family-wise Bonferroni at $\alpha{=}0.05$.
    25	
    26	    \item \textbf{Exploratory sweep} (20 tests, Benjamini--Hochberg FDR
    27	    at $q{=}0.10$): descriptive effect sizes for saturation fits, reward
    28	    proxies, and auxiliary probes. These are \emph{descriptive only}: no
    29	    claim in the abstract or Claim 1--4 table depends on an exploratory-sweep
    30	    $p$-value.
    31	
    32	    \item \textbf{Global battery} (38 tests): reported for completeness in
    33	    Appendix~\ref{sec:stat_rigor_updates}; not used for any abstract- or
    34	    claim-table level assertion.
    35	
    36	    \item \textbf{Trace-level non-independence caveat}: all per-step trace
    37	    statistics (first-10, last-10, 30-step series) are autocorrelated.
    38	    We therefore report them as \emph{descriptive effect sizes only} and
    39	    do not invoke them as inferential evidence. Any $p$-value attached to
    40	    a trace-derived quantity in the body text is reported for transparency,
    41	    not for claim certification.
    42	\end{enumerate}
    43	
    44	In short: Claim 1--4 rest on the 5-test primary family; everything else is
    45	descriptive.  This paragraph takes precedence over any narrower protocol
    46	statement elsewhere in the manuscript.
    47	
