   151	% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   152	\subsection{Carbon Footprint Estimation}
   153	\label{sec:carbon}
   154	% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   155	
   156	Table~\ref{tab:carbon2} computes an energy and CO$_2$-equivalent estimate
   157	for each platform. We follow the methodology of
   158	\citet{patterson2024empirical} and \citet{strubell2019energy}: for each
   159	GPU-hour we multiply device TDP by wall-clock GPU-hours and the data-centre
   160	Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE), then multiply by the grid carbon intensity
   161	in the region where the hardware is believed to be located.
   162	
   163	\paragraph{Assumed constants.}
   164	\begin{itemize}
   165	  \item NVIDIA H100 SXM5 TDP: 700\,W.
   166	  \item NVIDIA A100 80GB TDP: 400\,W.
   167	  \item NVIDIA L4 TDP: 72\,W.
   168	  \item NVIDIA T4 TDP: 70\,W.
   169	  \item Data-centre PUE: 1.1 (conservative; typical hyperscale PUE is
   170	        1.10--1.15 \cite{google2023pue, aws2023pue}).
   171	  \item US average grid intensity (EPA eGRID 2023): 0.367\,kg\,CO$_2$-eq / kWh
   172	        \cite{epa2023egrid}.
   173	  \item Indian average grid intensity (CEA 2023): 0.716\,kg\,CO$_2$-eq / kWh
   174	        \cite{cea2023co2}.
   175	  \item We use the US average for Modal H100 (US-East region as configured)
   176	        and Tinker (location undisclosed; assumed US), and the Indian
   177	        average for Colab Pro T4 used by authors based in Bengaluru
   178	        (Google Cloud asia-south1).
   179	\end{itemize}
   180	
   181	\paragraph{GPU-hour estimates.}
   182	Tinker GPU-hour counts are not disclosed by the platform. We estimate them
   183	from wall-clock run duration and assume a single H100-class accelerator per
   184	job, which is consistent with Tinker's published architecture for the
   185	model sizes we trained. Modal GPU-hours are measured directly from Modal's
   186	billing dashboard.
   187	
   188	\begin{table}[ht]
   189	\centering
   190	\small
   191	\caption{Energy and carbon footprint estimates. Tinker hardware is not
   192	publicly disclosed; we assume 1$\times$ H100 equivalent per run. Failed /
   193	stalled runs are included. Totals rounded to one significant figure.}
   194	\label{tab:carbon2}
   195	\begin{tabular}{lrrrrr}
   196	\toprule
   197	\textbf{Platform} & \textbf{GPU-h} & \textbf{TDP\,(W)} & \textbf{PUE} &
   198	\textbf{Energy\,(kWh)} & \textbf{CO$_2$\,(kg)} \\
   199	\midrule
   200	Tinker (assumed H100)   & \textasciitilde 950 & 700 & 1.1 & \textasciitilde 732 & \textasciitilde 269 \\
   201	Modal H100 (US-East)    & \textasciitilde 18  & 700 & 1.1 & \textasciitilde 14  & \textasciitilde 5.1 \\
   202	PES A100 (in-kind)      & \textasciitilde 60  & 400 & 1.1 & \textasciitilde 26  & \textasciitilde 19   \\
   203	Colab Pro T4 (asia-south1) & \textasciitilde 40 & 70 & 1.2 & \textasciitilde 3.4 & \textasciitilde 2.4  \\
   204	NVIDIA L4 (TRL baseline)   & \textasciitilde 10 & 72 & 1.1 & \textasciitilde 0.8 & \textasciitilde 0.3  \\
   205	\midrule
   206	\textbf{Project total (best estimate)} & & & & \textasciitilde 776 & \textasciitilde 296 \\
   207	\bottomrule
   208	\end{tabular}
   209	\end{table}
   210	
   211	\paragraph{Interpretation and uncertainty.}
   212	Our best estimate of \textasciitilde 296\,kg\,CO$_2$-eq for the entire
   213	project is comparable to a single round-trip economy flight
   214	Bengaluru--Delhi (\textasciitilde 300\,kg). The dominant uncertainty is
   215	the Tinker GPU-hour count: because Tinker does not expose hardware telemetry,
   216	a factor-of-two error in GPU-hours or TDP is plausible. Under a pessimistic
   217	assumption (2$\times$ GPU-hours, H100 running near 100\% TDP continuously),
   218	the Tinker contribution could be as high as \textasciitilde 540\,kg CO$_2$-eq.
   219	Under an optimistic assumption (Tinker backends actually use more
   220	energy-efficient accelerators than H100, 50\% average utilisation) the
   221	contribution could be as low as \textasciitilde 130\,kg. We report the
   222	central estimate in the main table and caution readers that it should not
   223	be interpreted as precise. \emph{All} numbers should be regarded as upper
   224	bounds on the carbon cost of reproducing our work, because subsequent
   225	users can skip unsuccessful attempts and optional ablation sweeps.
   226	
   227	\paragraph{Offset and mitigation.}
   228	We did not purchase carbon offsets. Instead, we have (a) released all
   229	trained checkpoints on HuggingFace Hub so that downstream users do not
   230	need to re-run our experiments; (b) released step-level CSV logs so that
   231	learning curves can be inspected without re-training; and (c) documented
   232	in Section~\ref{sec:compute_accounting} which runs were wasteful, so that
   233	replicators can skip them. We regard reproducibility-by-artefact as a
   234	more durable mitigation than offsets.
