   236	% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   237	\subsection{Data Provenance}
   238	\label{sec:provenance}
   239	% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   240	
   241	\ours{} uses only publicly released research datasets. No private data,
   242	personally identifiable information, or licensed proprietary content is
   243	used. No human annotators were employed during this work. We document
   244	each dataset below.
   245	
   246	\paragraph{GSM8K \cite{cobbe2021training}.}
   247	8{,}500 grade-school math word problems (7{,}473 train / 1{,}319 test)
   248	authored by human writers contracted by OpenAI. Released under the
   249	\textbf{MIT License} via \url{https://github.com/openai/grade-school-math}.
   250	We use the standard train/test splits without modification. The canonical
   251	citation is \citet{cobbe2021training}. Known limitations of GSM8K include
   252	gender-neutral but culturally US-centric word problems (names, currencies,
   253	sports) and a moderate rate of human-labelling errors estimated at
   254	\textasciitilde 2\% by \cite{zhang2024gsm1k}. Our held-out evaluation
   255	respects the test/train split.
   256	
   257	\paragraph{Salesforce xLAM-Function-Calling-60k \cite{liu2024xlam}.}
   258	60{,}000 function-calling examples generated by Salesforce Research as
   259	training data for the xLAM agentic model family. Released under the
   260	\textbf{CC BY 4.0} license via \url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/Salesforce/xlam-function-calling-60k}.
