   364	\subsection{Online GSM8K Training Rewards}
   365	\label{sec:main_results}
   366	
   367	This paper is an empirical audit of a heterogeneous run corpus, not a controlled
   368	algorithm benchmark. Most Tinker runs are single-seed, short-horizon, and
   369	evaluated by online training reward. We therefore use them to study reward
   370	dynamics, failure modes, and stack sensitivity. Capability claims are restricted
   371	to evaluations with held-out prompts and explicit base-model controls; under that
   372	standard, the GSM8K lift is small and non-significant. Table~\ref{tab:evidence_types}
   373	summarizes the evidence hierarchy used throughout the paper.
   374	
   375	\begin{table}[htbp]
   376	\centering
   377	\caption{Evidence types and permitted interpretations in this audit.}
   378	\label{tab:evidence_types_detail}
   379	\scriptsize
   380	\begin{tabular}{p{3.2cm}p{3.0cm}p{2.5cm}p{2.5cm}}
   381	\toprule
   382	\textbf{Evidence type} & \textbf{Runs} & \textbf{Independent unit} & \textbf{Can support} \\
   383	\midrule
   384	Tinker GRPO traces & Mostly single-seed, 30-step & run/checkpoint & descriptive dynamics only \\
   385	GSM8K held-out base-vs-GRPO & 5 seeds, 200 prompts & paired prompt/seed & narrow capability check; null result \\
   386	Top-checkpoint GSM8K audit & selected checkpoints, 500 prompts & checkpoint & selection/overfitting audit, not causal effect \\
   387	ZVF validation & 22 deduplicated runs & run & triage claim only \\
   388	Tool-use / HumanEval / MATH & proxy or harness-bound & task-specific trace & no broad capability claim \\
   389	\midrule
   390	\multicolumn{4}{p{11.2cm}}{\small \textit{Note:} Because many runs are single-seed and step-level rewards are autocorrelated within traces, we avoid treating per-step samples as independent experimental replicates. Inferential tests are reported only when the independent unit is a seed, prompt, or independently replicated run. Step-level reward samples inside a single training trace are treated as autocorrelated telemetry, not independent observations.} \\
   391	\bottomrule
   392	\end{tabular}
   393	\end{table}
