+# ARIS Round 3 -- Pre-submission Sanity Pass
+
+## 1. Overall Score
+6/10 (6=weak accept, 7=accept)
+
+## 2. Kill Argument
+The paper asks the reader to trust one narrow negative result as its only clean capability anchor, but that anchor is still internally inconsistent. The introduction states a paired GSM8K 200-example control (`sections/intro.tex:28-34`). The body then repeatedly describes the same control as a random 50-problem subset (`main_eai_body.tex:564, 587, 636, 1588, 1640, 1737`), while elsewhere calling it the same `N=200` held-out slice (`main_eai_body.tex:385, 645, 1590, 1656, 1735`; `ethics_statement.tex:392`). Worse, the reconciliation paragraph labels it both a paired control and “a one-sample test against the base” (`main_eai_body.tex:643-646`). A hostile reviewer can therefore say the paper’s central empirical anchor is not auditable: if the only clean held-out result is not specified consistently, then the negative transfer claim and the diagnostic framing built on it are not yet submission-safe.
+
+## 3. Weaknesses
+### CRITICAL
+- The single clean held-out GSM8K control still has two incompatible sample sizes and two incompatible test descriptions: `200` at `sections/intro.tex:29`, `main_eai_body.tex:385, 645, 1590, 1656, 1735`, `ethics_statement.tex:392`; `50` at `main_eai_body.tex:564, 587, 636, 1588, 1640, 1737`. `main_eai_body.tex:643-646` also says “paired” and “one-sample” for the same analysis.
+
+### MAJOR
+- The toy arithmetic cross-library baseline is still in the main Results (`main_eai_body.tex:509-549`) and remains promoted in the statistical appendix tables (`sections/stat_rigor_updates.tex:87-104`), which invites a “toy-task inflation” rejection line.
+- The stack-sensitivity headline still depends on only two real cross-stack runs while `verl` and `OpenRLHF` remain dry-run placeholders (`sections/abstract_eai.tex:12-14`, `main_eai_body.tex:490-492`).
+- Bibliography cleanup is not submission-grade: duplicate works and malformed entry types remain, so Vancouver compliance is not fully clean (`references.bib:237-256, 542-583, 776-789, 1195-1200, 1435-1440, 1599-1604`).
+
+### MINOR
+- High-overlap slogan-like sentences remain and are worth rewriting before Turnitin.
+- Most likely EAI width hotspots are `tab:main_results_stats` (`sections/stat_rigor_updates.tex:60-84`), `tab:ppo_grpo_stats` (`sections/stat_rigor_updates.tex:141-156`), `tab:results_gsm8k_stats` (`sections/stat_rigor_updates.tex:114-138`), `tab:results_arithmetic_stats` (`sections/stat_rigor_updates.tex:87-104`), and `tab:heldout_gsm8k` (`main_eai_body.tex:605-631`).
+
+## 4. Actionable Fixes (surgical, 1-line each)
+- `{file: main_eai_body.tex, line: 643-646, exact change: replace with one canonical protocol sentence: "The 82.0%->83.3% control uses a fixed held-out slice of N=<final> prompts, 5 seeds, and a paired per-prompt analysis against the same base-model outputs."}`
+- `{file: sections/intro.tex, line: 29-30, exact change: replace "200-example" with the same canonical N used everywhere else.}`
+- `{file: main_eai_body.tex, line: 564, exact change: delete "(evaluated on a random 50-problem subset)" unless the final protocol is truly N=50; do not mention both 50 and 200 anywhere.}`
+- `{file: main_eai_body.tex, line: 587, exact change: same cleanup as line 564.}`
+- `{file: main_eai_body.tex, line: 1588-1590, exact change: collapse the 50/200 split into one sentence with one N and one test description.}`
+- `{file: main_eai_body.tex, line: 1656, exact change: rewrite as "A clean held-out GSM8K control (Qwen3-8B, 5 seeds, N=<final> prompts) shows 82.0%->83.3% (p=0.26)."}` 
+- `{file: ethics_statement.tex, line: 392-393, exact change: match the same canonical held-out protocol wording used in the main body.}`
+- `{file: main_eai_body.tex, line: 509-549, exact change: move the entire "Cross-Library Comparison" subsection to an appendix section titled "Arithmetic Sanity Baseline Across RL Libraries".}`
+- `{file: main_eai_body.tex, line: 551-560, exact change: add one caveat sentence after the subsection opener: "The arithmetic sanity baseline is reported in the appendix because it is a toy stack-mismatch diagnostic, not part of the paper's main empirical claim."}`
+- `{file: references.bib, line: 11-17/152-158/237-256/577-583/776-789/1195-1200/1435-1440/1599-1604, exact change: delete duplicate keys and convert malformed records to the correct BibTeX type with proper venue/journal fields.}`
+
+## 5. Bibliography Surgery
+- Keys to delete (duplicate sets): [`cobbe2021gsm8k`, `christiano2017deep`, `kaplan2020scaling`]
+- Keys to fix (wrong type / missing field): [`schulman2017proximal`, `sedghpour2024artifact`, `azar2024ipo`, `zhang2025verifybench`, `luong2024reft`, `havrilla2023trlx`]
+
+## 6. Held-out n Locations
+Distinct sample sizes still referenced for the GSM8K held-out control: `2` (`50`, `200`).
+
+- `sections/intro.tex:29` -> `200`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:385` -> `200`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:564` -> `50`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:587` -> `50`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:636` -> `50`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:645` -> `200`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:1588` -> `50`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:1590` -> `200`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:1640` -> `50`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:1656` -> `200` and `50`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:1735` -> `200`
+- `main_eai_body.tex:1737` -> `50`
+- `ethics_statement.tex:392` -> `200`
+
+## 7. Plagiarism Flags (up to 6)
+High-overlap risk, not a plagiarism accusation:
+
+- `"The algorithm label alone is an under-specified experimental treatment; usable signal must be verified per stack."` — `sections/abstract_eai.tex:15-16`
+- `"This paper audits a group-relative RL runner inspired by GRPO, not a canonical GRPO reproduction."` — `sections/intro.tex:18-19`
+- `"The familiar p_x > 1/G rule is only an expected-one-success heuristic; it is not a threshold theorem."` — `sections/intro.tex:76-77`
+- `"The mixed-group probability formula is the explanatory core; ZVF/GU is the operational interface."` — `sections/intro.tex:97-98`
+- `"The paper's main contribution is therefore diagnostic."` — `sections/conclusion.tex:28`
+- `"A bare ``PPO versus GRPO'' comparison is not an interpretable scientific claim."` — `sections/conclusion.tex:53-54`
+
+## 8. EAI Compliance
+- abstract length (chars): 865
+- keyword count: 8
+- vancouver: false
+- structured abstract: true
+
+## 9. Verdict
+Almost — the paper is close, but the single clean held-out protocol and bibliography still need one consistency pass before submission.
